.TH CCIRCQ_RECV 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccircq_recv \- receive a message (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval ccircq_recv(ccircq *cq, cmessage *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Waits until a message is in the queue and hands it over in
target_buf, without copying the data. The data then belongs to the
caller, who must free target_buf->data when done with it.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq          Circular queue to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message together with the ownership
            of the data.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - A message was received. The caller must free
                      target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args   - cq or target_buf is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The wait has no time limit. Turning sends off doesn't wake a waiting
receiver: It stays blocked until sends are turned on again and a
message arrives. The function is thread-safe.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccircq_try_recv (3),
.BR ccircq_timed_recv (3),
.BR ccircq_send (3)
